Fix libmicrohttpd build on the PS4 payload SDK (orbis-clang,
--host=x86_64-pc-freebsd).

The SDK's libc exports the symbol cpuset_getaffinity(), so configure defines
HAVE_CPUSET_GETAFFINITY=1. However the SDK provides neither <sys/cpuset.h>
nor <sys/_cpuset.h> (HAVE_SYS_CPUSET_H and HAVE_SYS__CPUSET_H are both left
undefined), so the cpuset_t type is never declared. The FreeBSD-style
cpuset_getaffinity() branch then fails to compile:

    mhd_tool_get_cpu_count.c:199:5: error: unknown type name 'cpuset_t';
      did you mean 'cpusetid_t'?

Only compile the cpuset_getaffinity() path when the header that actually
declares cpuset_t is present. When it is not, MHD falls back to the
sysctl(HW_NCPU) / sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN) detection methods, both of
which the PS4 SDK supports.

Apply from the libmicrohttpd source root with:
    patch -p1 < libmicrohttpd-ps4-cpuset.patch
or:
    git apply libmicrohttpd-ps4-cpuset.patch

--- a/src/tools/mhd_tool_get_cpu_count.c
+++ b/src/tools/mhd_tool_get_cpu_count.c
@@ -192,7 +192,12 @@
 mhd_tool_get_proc_cpu_count_cpuset_getaffinity_ (void)
 {
   int ret = -1;
-#if defined(HAVE_CPUSET_GETAFFINITY)
+/* The cpuset_t type lives in <sys/cpuset.h> (or <sys/_cpuset.h>). Some
+   toolchains (e.g. the PS4 payload SDK) export cpuset_getaffinity() without
+   providing that header, so guard on the header as well as the function to
+   avoid an "unknown type name 'cpuset_t'" compile error. */
+#if defined(HAVE_CPUSET_GETAFFINITY) \
+  && (defined(HAVE_SYS_CPUSET_H) || defined(HAVE_SYS__CPUSET_H))
   /* FreeBSD style */
   if (0 >= ret)
   {
